use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component Stepper:
    description:
        A stepper changes a number up or down by a fixed amount using a pair
        of buttons, such as − and + next to a quantity. It stays between a
        minimum and a maximum, and each button is disabled at its end.

    value:
        It shows the current number. Typing a number in directly is a
        NumberInput, not a stepper.

    pointer:
        Pressing a button changes the number by one step. Holding it down keeps
        changing it until the user lets go.

    keyboard:
        The stepper is a single stop in the Tab order, not one per button. Once
        focused, the Up and Down arrow keys raise and lower the number. Home
        and End jump to the minimum and maximum.

    bounds:
        At the minimum, the decrease button is disabled; at the maximum, the
        increase button is. The number never goes past either.

    name:
        The stepper has a name saying what it counts, such as "Guests".
        Assistive tools read out the new number each time it changes.
